{"id":117,"name":"seadra","speciesId":117,"dex":117,"form":"normal","generation":1,"types":["water"],"stats":{"hp":55,"attack":65,"defense":95,"special-attack":95,"special-defense":45,"speed":85},"abilities":[{"name":"poison-point","hidden":false},{"name":"sniper","hidden":false},{"name":"damp","hidden":true}],"height":12,"weight":250,"baseExp":154,"sprites":{"normal":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/117.png","shiny":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/shiny/117.png","icon":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/117.png"},"cry":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/cries/main/cries/pokemon/latest/117.ogg","genus":"Dragon Pokémon","genusPt":"Pokémon Dragão","flavor":[{"version":"red","text":"Capable of swim­ ming backwards by rapidly flapping its wing-like pectoral fins and stout tail."},{"version":"yellow","text":"Touching the back fin causes numb­ ness. It hooks its tail to coral to stay in place while sleeping."},{"version":"gold","text":"An examination of its cells revealed the presence of a gene not found in HORSEA. It became a hot topic."},{"version":"silver","text":"Its fin-tips leak poison. Its fins and bones are highly valued as ingredients in herbal medicine."},{"version":"crystal","text":"The male raises the young. If it is approached, it uses its toxic spikes to fend off the intruder."},{"version":"ruby","text":"SEADRA sleeps after wriggling itself between the branches of coral. Those trying to harvest coral are occasionally stung by this POKéMON’s poison barbs if they fail to notice it."},{"version":"sapphire","text":"SEADRA generates whirlpools by spinning its body. The whirlpools are strong enough to swallow even fishing boats. This POKéMON weakens prey with these currents, then swallows it whole."},{"version":"emerald","text":"The poisonous barbs all over its body are highly valued as ingredients for making traditional herbal medicine. It shows no mercy to anything approaching its nest."},{"version":"firered","text":"Its body bristles with sharp spikes. Carelessly trying to touch it could cause fainting from the spikes."},{"version":"leafgreen","text":"It is capable of swimming backwards by rapidly flapping its winglike pectoral fins and stout tail."},{"version":"diamond","text":"Its spines provide protection. Its fins and bones are prized as traditional medicine ingredients."},{"version":"black-2","text":"Its spines provide protection. Its fins and bones are prized as traditional-medicine ingredients."},{"version":"omega-ruby","text":"Seadra sleeps after wriggling itself between the branches of coral. Those trying to harvest coral are occasionally stung by this Pokémon’s poison barbs if they fail to notice it."},{"version":"alpha-sapphire","text":"Seadra generates whirlpools by spinning its body. The whirlpools are strong enough to swallow even fishing boats. This Pokémon weakens prey with these currents, then swallows it whole."},{"version":"lets-go-pikachu","text":"Touching the back fin causes numbness. It hooks its tail to coral to stay in place while sleeping."},{"version":"sword","text":"It’s the males that raise the offspring. While Seadra are raising young, the spines on their backs secrete thicker and stronger poison."},{"version":"shield","text":"Seadra’s mouth is slender, but its suction power is strong. In an instant, Seadra can suck in food that’s larger than the opening of its mouth."}],"flavorPt":"A boca de Seadra é delgada, mas seu poder de sucção é forte. Em um instante, Seadra pode sugar alimentos maiores que a abertura de sua boca.","genderRate":4,"captureRate":75,"eggGroups":["water1","dragon"],"isLegendary":false,"isMythical":false,"evolution":{"species":"horsea","speciesId":116,"evolvesTo":[{"conditions":["Nível 32"],"species":"seadra","speciesId":117,"evolvesTo":[{"conditions":["Troca, Segurando Dragon Scale"],"species":"kingdr